From 01cd11b737911764f2a4ff2a6afc3bc033ef5043 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:01:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] BackgroundInfoLoader: the loading flag is atomic too

The loader thread clears m_bIsLoading at the end of Run() (Reset())
while the thread of the window reads it (IsLoading()), and Load() sets
it from a third. It was a volatile bool, which orders nothing between
threads: ThreadSanitizer reports the race in three tests of
TestBackgroundInfoLoader, among them Piers e80c433 (an item held
twice), on every run. Hades made m_bStop atomic for the same reason in
6ff97e3; this does the same for the other flag. Its three uses read and
write it as before.
---
 xbmc/BackgroundInfoLoader.h | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/BackgroundInfoLoader.h b/xbmc/BackgroundInfoLoader.h
index e45cb74..3f96d35 100644
--- a/xbmc/BackgroundInfoLoader.h
+++ b/xbmc/BackgroundInfoLoader.h
@@ -88,7 +88,9 @@ protected:
   std::vector<CFileItemPtr> m_vecItems; // FileItemList would delete the items and we only want to keep a reference.
   CCriticalSection m_lock;
 
-  volatile bool m_bIsLoading{false};
+  //! Hades: atomic, as the loader thread clears it (Reset()) while another thread reads it
+  //! (IsLoading())
+  std::atomic<bool> m_bIsLoading{false};
   //! Hades: atomic, as StopAsync() sets it from one thread while the loader thread reads it
   std::atomic<bool> m_bStop{true};
   /*!
